      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To discuss the effect of electroacupuncture at Chengshan (BL 57) on postoperative pain of mixed hemorrhoids."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "One hundred and twenty cases with postoperative pain of mixed hemorrhoids were divided into an electroacupuncture group (60 cases) and a medication group (60 cases) randomly. The disperse-dense wave in frequency of 2Hz/100Hz at Chengshan (BL 57) were used in the electroacupuncture group. Its first treatment was in 30 min after the operation, and then it was given once a day after hip bath in the morning. 2 tablets of Naproxen Sunstained Release Capsule were taken in 30 min after operation in the medication group, and then it was taken 2 tablets a day before dressing change. After 4 times of treatment, evaluate the changing condition of Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) at 5 h, 24 h, 48 h and 72 h after operation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The VAS at 5 h, 24 h, 48 h and 72 h after operation in the electroacupuncture group (6.78 +/- 2.12, 5.56 +/- 1.87, 4.34 +/- 2.23 and 3.15 +/- 2.11) were all lower than those in the medication group (7.56 +/- 2.01, 6.23 +/- 1.15, 5.57 +/- 2.21 and 4.34 +/- 2.12), and the difference was statistically significant (all P < 0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Electroacupuncture at Chengshan (BL 57) can reduce the postoperative pain of mixed hemorrhoids."
        }
      ]},
